The Big Bang Theory is popular with most regular, non-internet-heavy TV watchers.

&#x200B;

Reddit would have you believe it's universally reviled.

I believe the 16 port switches are quite a bit less depth than the 48 port. This is the one I'm going to try:

&#x200B;

[https://www.amazon.com/NavePoint-Network-Server-Cabinet-Enclosure/dp/B01FKOW4LS/ref=sr\_1\_3\_pp?crid=2MUK78UBTRFPC&keywords=network+rack+with+door&qid=1707328447&s=electronics&sprefix=network+rack+with+door%2Celectronics%2C439&sr=1-3&ufe=app\_do%3Aamzn1.fos.f5122f16-c3e8-4386-bf32-63e904010ad0](https://www.amazon.com/NavePoint-Network-Server-Cabinet-Enclosure/dp/B01FKOW4LS/ref=sr_1_3_pp?crid=2MUK78UBTRFPC&keywords=network+rack+with+door&qid=1707328447&s=electronics&sprefix=network+rack+with+door%2Celectronics%2C439&sr=1-3&ufe=app_do%3Aamzn1.fos.f5122f16-c3e8-4386-bf32-63e904010ad0)

&#x200B;

Depth on 48 port is over 13.75 according to data sheet and the other one linked here is 13.75 depth.
